From ecbe848df07bb58b37ab41fbcc3b87be9acb3c4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: weles <weles@local>
Date: Fri, 17 Apr 2026 21:52:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Weles modifications rebased onto Chromium 147.0.7727.108

Cherry-picked weles-145 HEAD (6d3e502726301) onto 147.0.7727.108
(e74a8f5bfafeb). 4 files had real merge conflicts, resolved:

- third_party/blink/public/common/switches.h: kept 147's new
  kXSLTEnabledPolicy alongside weles's kWelesFingerprint.
- third_party/blink/common/switches.cc: same (kept both decls).
- third_party/blink/renderer/core/execution_context/navigator_base.cc:
  kept weles_fingerprint_config.h include.
- chrome/browser/ui/browser_manager_service.cc: kept 147's new
  pop-and-erase Shutdown pattern (it already handles the raw_ptr<Browser>
  dangling issue weles fixed separately) AND injected weles's
  per-browser OnBrowserClosed notify call so GlobalBrowserCollection
  drops its raw_ptr<BrowserWindowInterface> before Browser destructor
  runs (the SIGSEGV-in-metrics-flush issue is distinct from the
  raw_ptr<Browser> one).
